there's an investment scam I want to  talk to you about today which has  actually been around for a while but  it's really grown lately because of its  association with Donald Trump and this  is a general type of investment scam  called the foreign currency scam but the  one I'm going to talk about today in  particular centers around a practically  worthless currency the Iraqi currency  the Iraqi dinar the premise is this  right now  the Iraqi currency is really undervalued  so say the evangelists or some people  call them scammers so as a result it's a  really great investment opportunity if  you buy some of these Iraqi dinars now  with US dollars all you need to do is  wait until Iraq revalue the currency at  which point you'll make a huge profit by  exchanging the dinars back for US  dollars so to set up the math of it  right now one u.s. dollar is right  around 1200 Iraqi dinars or to say it a  different way one dinar is worth about  point zero zero zero eight four dollars  okay or point zero eight four cents per  dollar the people that are promoting  this scam claim that once the currency  revalue Zoar rvs as they call it one  dinar could be worth as much as three or  four US dollars or almost five thousand  times more valuable than it is right now  this seems like most currency investment  opportunities you buy now that currency  becomes more valuable you cash out and  it's a big win but the key here is that  there's something about the Iraqi dinar  that will in particular make it very  quickly increase in value so that in a  way that is connected with political  decisions or political circumstances and  we'll get to exactly what those are in a  second before this before the Trump era  the Denari ins have been saying that  this revaluation is just about to happen  it's gonna happen any day they've been  saying this for years at least since  2012 and if you check out the dinar guru  which is an online forum about the dinar  26% believe that this revaluation is  just days away  74% believe that quote the dinar will  not change until certain things are  accomplished and that will get us to why  this is growing so much right now if you  google Iraqi dinar the top results are  all forums that focus on this currency  scam like dinar guru the websites are  filled with all these little tidbits of  information about the political  situation the economic situation in Iraq  a lot of them are updated multiple times  per day the facts are very much  cherry-picked to make the readers feel  like this is on the verge of happening  this revaluation is is almost there it's  gonna happen any moment now and it's all  meant to get people to invest right away  without much research into this out of  fear of missing out on this great  revaluation and it also encourages  people who own dinars to keep holding  them this has been a known scam for a  while if you go back to 2013 the Better  Business Bureau specifically names the  Iraqi dinar as a currency that's often  sold in these foreign currency scams  along with the Vietnamese dong and the  Egyptian pound in October of 2018 the  Justice Department in Atlanta  successfully prosecuted the co-owners  and the chief operating officer of one  of the largest Iraqi dinar exchanges in  the United States convicting them a  fraud the business they ran was worth  over six hundred million dollars in 2015  federal attorneys for the Northern  District of Ohio tried and sentenced the  man to prison for running a fraud scheme  worth over 24 million dollars which  included selling Iraqi dinars  technically it's illegal to sell an  investment opportunity to the public  without a license but many of the dinars  sellers are operating because of a  technical a legal technicality we could  call it it's technically legal to sell  currencies if and only if they're  considered to be collector or novelty  items the other way that businesses are  able to legally operate is by  registering as money service businesses  MSBs  with the US Treasury Department this is  just one form you have to fill out very  little oversight as  actually happening the reason which we  are now getting to that this scam has  exploded recently is Donald Trump  because Trump was rumored to be an  investor in the iraqi dinar himself so  when Trump was elected in 2016 the scam  was revitalized with the idea that  Donald Trump's policy in order to enrich  himself which actually is not  far-fetched that he would do policy to  enrich himself would include the  revaluation of the dinar there's a 20-17  press conference where Trump actually  said that soon all currencies will be  quote on a level playing field a very  vague statement but when Trump said this  he was probably talking about Chinese  currency and the trade imbalance with  China but the Denari ins interpreted or  claimed to believe for the purposes of  pumping their scam that Trump was  talking about maybe revaluing the dinar  trumpets and Denari ins are two  different groups but there's overlap  between the two will summer has a great  article in The Daily Beast called Trump  fans sink savings into Iraqi dinar scam  which shows that many investors in the  scheme are also big Trump fans many of  them tweet about q and on one minute and  then about dinar revaluation the next to  understand why people could be led to  believe that this worthless currency is  actually on the cusp of an extreme  revaluation we've got to take a quick  look at the past few decades of Iraqi  history the current exchange rate as I  mentioned between the dollar and the  dinar is about one to twelve hundred  this means that if you went to Iraq  tomorrow and exchanged a hundred US  dollars for dinars you would get about a  hundred and twenty thousand dinar back  but the exchange rate wasn't always like  this if you go back to 1988 the exchange  rate was one dinar to three dollars and  22 cents meaning that a hundred US  dollars in Iraq in 1988 would be worth  31 dinars in return things changed when  Saddam Hussein invaded Kuwait and by  late 1995 after that invasion and the  first Iraq war  the value of the dinar was down to one  dollar being worth roughly 3,000 dinar  things have gotten worse since the u.s.  invaded Iraq under false pretenses in  2003 and since then Iraq has been  continuously embroiled in insurgency and  civil strife which anyone who's been  following politics is aware of civil war  instability these are not good things  for a nation's economy and although  things have started to improve somewhat  recently in Iraq it's still precarious  Iraq is still engaged in the war against  Isis it's government is in a very  tenuous political position at best and  oftentimes people who are invested in  this scam like to bring up the example  of the Kuwaiti dinar which after the  Gulf War did actually experience a  pretty significant revaluation the  country is also Iraq's neighbor so it  might seem sort of superficially  reasonable but this is a misleading  comparison number one Kuwait's a much  wealthier country than iraq massive oil  reserves much bigger than Iraq's it also  has far fewer people to take care of 3  million in Kuwait vs. 33 million in Iraq  although Kuwait suffered damage to its  people and its infrastructure when  Saddam invaded that pales in comparison  to 15 years of constant war and constant  instability in Iraq much of it brought  by the United States with its invasion  in 2003 and even today Iraq still needs  to contend with the threat of civil war  which Kuwait did not have to deal with  the other important reality ignored by  the Denari ins is that such a  revaluation that they are saying could  happen any day would immediately be  harmful to the Iraqi economy and it  would only undermine the Iraqi  government's ability to pay its own  debts because an increase in the value  of its currency would make their  extensive government debt even more  expensive to repay and with the country  still requiring loans from the IMF and  other international financial bodies  just to maintain current spending levels  there's no incentive for the government  to push for that revaluation one reason  that the dinars scam feels real to many  people is that when you invest in it you  think you're getting something of real  tangible value a valuable asset on  YouTube right now there are an untold  number of videos of people excitedly  unboxing their shipments full of dinar  but the problem is that the dinar is not  even worth the paper it's printed on  outside of Iraq the only reason that  having dinar would be useful to any  American consumer would be if they were  traveling to Iraq not something that  many Americans are doing outside of  Iraq's borders there are no currency  exchange houses or banks that are  willing to exchange dinar for dollars  since no exchange exists dinar dealers  are able to charge whatever price they  want when you want to buy these dinars  or when you want to sell them the spread  between the buy and sell price is often  up to 20% which is outrageous compared  to any other stable or even remotely  stable currency so even if you say you  know what I'm going to cut my losses and  sell the dinar back immediately I made a  mistake you can lose up to 20% of your  investment instantly even without any  change in the currencies valuation these  denarian czar modern-day snake oil  salesmen but instead of curing physical  ailments this investment of only a few  thousand dollars is sold as potentially  curing all of your financial woes and  leaving you very rich of course it's not  going to happen and the Trump presidency  is only making the scam even more  prevalent
 

